          "name": "Frozen chemistry perception layer",
          "description": "Keep existing chemistry predictors fixed so that the first experimental phase tests only the proposed planning mechanism. Candidate retrosynthetic disconnections are generated by a template-free graph-to-sequence retrosynthesis model [Author et al., 2021](https://openalex.org/W3206796875) or a mechanism-driven retrosynthesis framework [Author et al., 2022](https://openalex.org/W4308632600). Reaction outcome feasibility is scored with a chemistry-aware bond-change model [Author et al., 2024](https://openalex.org/W4392515737), and selectivity-sensitive steps are scored with a meta-learning model for asymmetric catalysis [Author et al., 2025](https://openalex.org/W4409453348). The predictor outputs are calibrated with ensembles or conformal prediction, but the predictors are not retrained during the primary hypothesis test."
        },
        {
          "name": "Mechanistic incompatibility latent graph",
          "description": "Construct a discrete latent-variable graph over hidden mechanistic states, including reaction-center electron-flow compatibility, protecting-group occupancy, chemoselectivity masks, catalyst-poison presence, stereochemical integrity, and side-reaction susceptibility. Variables are attached to molecular fragments and persist across retrosynthetic steps. Edges encode mechanism-induced dependencies, such as a deprotection revealing a nucleophile that later competes with an electrophile, a residual base that erodes stereochemistry, or a sulfur-containing impurity that poisons a later asymmetric hydrogenation catalyst. This structured representation extends mechanism-aware retrosynthesis [Author et al., 2022](https://openalex.org/W4308632600) and chemistry-aware bond-change modeling [Author et al., 2024](https://openalex.org/W4392515737) from single-step plausibility to route-level correlated failure modeling."
