        {
          "name": "Neuro-symbolic belief updater",
          "description": "Convert continuous predictor probabilities and uncertainty estimates into likelihoods over the discrete mechanistic variables, then update posterior beliefs after each observed or diagnostic result. This adapts neuro-symbolic bridging of uncertain continuous perception and discrete symbolic planning [Author et al., 2025](https://openalex.org/W7106207643). The continuous layer contains predictor scores for feasibility, yield, and selectivity, while the symbolic layer contains mechanistic predicates, protecting-group states, chemoselectivity constraints, and route feasibility constraints. The output is a route-level belief state rather than a single point estimate."
        },
        {
          "name": "Correlated route-risk planner",
          "description": "Score each candidate route by marginalizing route success over the mechanistic latent graph instead of multiplying independent step probabilities. Use a fixed mechanism-conditioned risk objective, such as CVaR over latent incompatibility factors, purification-aware yield risk, and enantioselectivity-tail constraints. This adapts probabilistic planning under uncertainty [Author et al., 2017](https://openalex.org/W7048571973) to retrosynthetic search and allows the planner to penalize routes whose steps share hidden failure causes, even when each step appears locally plausible."
        },
        {
          "name": "Diagnostic experiment selector",
          "description": "When route uncertainty is dominated by a small set of latent mechanistic variables, propose minimal diagnostic experiments, such as a small-scale test reaction, a protecting-group stability assay, a catalyst compatibility check, or an analytical stereochemical probe. Select diagnostics by expected value of information for route utility, then update the belief state and replan. This makes uncertainty reduction target mechanism-level feasibility rather than generic outcome observation, following probabilistic decision-theoretic planning under uncertainty [Author et al., 2017](https://openalex.org/W7048571973)."
        }
